course: dictionary
lesson: 15745
title: Treason and betrayal
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: Treason is a very serious word. It is the crime of betraying your own country, for example by helping its enemies or trying to overthrow its ruler or government. «Helping the enemy in a war is treason.» The clues are betray, which means to turn against someone, and enemy, which means someone who wants to harm you.
explain: Treason can also mean any great betrayal of trust. «When Sam told the whole class her secret, Ana felt it was treason.» Nobody went to war here, but a friend broke a promise so badly that it felt like a crime. Ask yourself: what word would fit? Betrayal fits, so treason means a very serious betrayal.
explain: Look out for phrases such as «high treason», «commit treason» and «charged with treason». Each one shows that treason is a crime that people can be accused of and tried for. When you see these phrases, think about serious betrayal.
fact: Treason means betraying your own country, or betraying a great trust.
fact: In the Gunpowder Plot of 1605, «Guy Fawkes» was caught and tried for treason.
fact: Treason is one of the most serious crimes there is.
fact: In the past, treason was punished by death.
fact: «Betray» means to turn against someone who trusted you, and this is the root idea of treason.
exercise: «Guy Fawkes was charged with treason after the Gunpowder Plot.» What kind of crime is treason? | Stealing sweets from a shop | *Betraying your own country | Running too fast on the playground | Forgetting your homework
exercise: «When Sam told the whole class her secret, Ana felt it was treason.» What does treason mean here? | A school trip to the museum | A war between two countries | A type of fancy cake | *A great betrayal of trust
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Helping the enemy in a war is treason.» that names the people who want to harm you in war. | treason | war | *enemy | helping
test: Mia says treason is just a bit of naughtiness. What is the right meaning? | Treason is a game played at parties | *Treason is a very serious betrayal, such as betraying your country | Treason means a loud noise | Treason means being late for school
test: Which example shows treason in the sense of a great betrayal of trust? | *Telling your best friend's secret to everyone | Sharing your lunch with a classmate | Finishing your homework early | Helping your friend with maths
exam: Why was Guy Fawkes charged with treason in 1605? | He painted a portrait of the King | He lost his school bag on the train | He sang too loudly in church | *He took part in a plot against the King and Parliament
